        "id": "cgei-ai-121-1-loader",
        "kind": "prose",
        "title": "Windowed raster loaders",
        "body": "Large rasters are rarely loaded whole into training loops. Read spatial windows (patches) with known row/column offsets, height and width. Preserve band order, dtype, scale, nodata and CRS/transform metadata so every sample stays georeferenced. Reject windows that are out of bounds, dominated by nodata, contain NaNs, or lack a matching label. Keep imagery, masks and labels in lockstep—silent dropping of only one side creates silent misalignment."
