        "body": "A Dataset yields samples; a DataLoader assembles batches. Batch size trades memory against throughput and gradient noise. Measure time spent waiting on the next batch versus time in the training step: if the accelerator idles, storage or decode is the bottleneck; if memory grows with workers, reduce concurrency or cache less. Prefetching and more workers help only when I/O is the limiter—they can worsen contention on slow disks. Never optimise throughput by weakening spatial train/test separation."
